Figure 5 illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Flow cytometry dot plots and histograms show that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone is minimally internalized, the presence of Nano-11-adsorbed OVA leads to a substantial increase in OVA within BMDCs. This indicates that Nano-11 effectively delivers antigens to dendritic cells, promoting efficient internalization of negatively charged proteins, which is crucial for its adjuvant effect in vaccine formulations.